# `const: @(Model m @ Model 3)`: a reference declaration whose candidate is one value and one more is refused at the
# extra value, whether or not anything reads the name (DECLARATION-CANDIDATE-ROLE, steps/defects.md). It was taken
# for a machine local with the model; the statement was refused at its start ("root operation not walkable yet: this
# statement").
Model:
    int: value 7
end: Model
fn: check () int
    const: @(Model m @ Model 3)
    return: 7
end: check
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: check(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
